#This is a sample file distributed with Galaxy that enables tools
#to use a directory of metagenomics files.
#Tab separated with 4 columns (value, name, dbkey, path):
# - value: stable identity of the data, "<database>-<build>-<artifact name>"
#          (for utility mappings additionally the mapping file name and suffix),
#          never contains an install date, because workflows serialize it
#          e.g. utility_mapping-full-map_go_uniref90-full_mapping_v201901b.txt
# - name:  human readable label shown in the tool form
# - dbkey: the HUMAnN version the entry was installed for (provenance,
#          the data itself is the same for HUMAnN 3.1.1 - 3.9)
# - path:  absolute path of the database directory (or of the mapping file)
#The artifact name is the name HUMAnN advertises for the bundle, see
#`humann_databases --available`, without the archive suffix. HUMAnN checks the
#version strings in the file names of the installed data, so the bundles must
#be used unmodified.
#Every HUMAnN 3.x release uses the same 201901b mapping bundle. The file
#name (map_go_uniref90, map_go_name, ...) selects one of the ~20 mappings.

utility_mapping-full-map_go_uniref90-full_mapping_v201901b.txt	Mapping (full) for Gene Ontology (GO) from UniRef90 (full_mapping_v201901b)	3.9	/path/to/data/map_go_uniref90.txt
